  "question": {
    "text": "The vapour density of N<sub>2</sub>O<sub>4</sub> at a certain temperature is 30. What is the percentage dissociation of N<sub>2</sub>O<sub>4</sub> at this temperature ?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "53.3 %",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "106.6 %",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "26.7 %",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "None of these",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "The reaction is<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>N</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <msub> <mtext>O</mtext> <mn>4</mn> </msub> <mo>⇌</mo> <mn>2</mn> <msub> <mtext>NO</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> </math><br /><br />mol. wt. of N<sub>2</sub>O<sub>4</sub><sub> </sub>= 14 x 2 + 16 x 4 = 92<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>∴&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo> </mrow> </math> Vapour density (D) of N<sub>2</sub>O<sub>4</sub> = 92/2 = 46<br /><br />We know that,<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mi>α</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>D</mtext> <mo>-</mo> <mtext>d</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>n</mtext> <mo>-</mo> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </mfenced> <mtext>d</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>4</mn> <mn>6</mn> <mo>-</mo> <mn>3</mn> <mn>0</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <mo>-</mo> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </mfenced> <mn>3</mn> <mn>0</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mn>6</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>3</mn> <mn>0</mn> </mrow></mfrac></mrow></math><br /><br />where,<br><br>D = Initial vapour density of reactant<br><br>d = vapour density of equilibrium mixture<br><br><math> <mi>&#x03B1;</mi></math>= degree of dissociation<br><br><math> <mrow> <mo>∴&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo> <mi>α</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mtext>0.533</mtext> </mrow> </math><br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <math> <mrow> <mo>=&nbsp;</mo> <mtext>53.3 %</mtext> </mrow> </math>"
  }
